From: OmarAfet (prepared with an LLM; see README)
Subject: [PATCH] rustc_span: do not compute line and column in `span_to_filename`

`SourceMap::span_to_filename` called `lookup_char_pos`, which also computes the
line, the column and the display column. The display column walks every char from
the start of the line to the position (`char_width` per char). Only the file name is
used, so this work is thrown away.

`Session::resolve_path` calls `span_to_filename` for every relative
`include_bytes!`, `include_str!` and `include!`. In generated code where a whole file
is one long line, each call walks up to the full line, so the total cost is
(number of calls) x (line length).

Measured with nightly-2026-10-14 (822182db4) on an Apple M2:
- test crate, 1,511 relative `include_bytes!` in one 2.4 MB line: expand_crate 8.2 s;
  same code with one call per line, or with absolute paths: 0.04 s.
- SteelMC `steel-registry` (17 MB generated code, 1,511 `include_bytes!`):
  about 90% of the macro-expansion samples are in this call chain
  (expand_include_bytes -> resolve_path -> span_to_filename ->
  lookup_file_pos_with_col_display -> char_width).

`lookup_char_pos(pos).file` is `lookup_source_file(pos)`, so the result is the same
file name; only the unused line and column work is removed.

---
 compiler/rustc_span/src/source_map.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/rustc_span/src/source_map.rs b/compiler/rustc_span/src/source_map.rs
--- a/compiler/rustc_span/src/source_map.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_span/src/source_map.rs
@@ -518,5 +518,6 @@
 
     pub fn span_to_filename(&self, sp: Span) -> FileName {
-        self.lookup_char_pos(sp.lo()).file.name.clone()
+        // Only the file is needed: skip the line and column lookup in `lookup_char_pos`.
+        self.lookup_source_file(sp.lo()).name.clone()
     }
 
